+# Dormant original offered-call custody
+
+Work in progress; not a production tool/service, RoleSourceLease or qualification.
+
+The only offer constructor and thread/start offer wrapper are cfg(test). Ordinary production starts and unsupported item/tool/call behavior remain unchanged. Test activation requires the actual complete-written original thread/start, native validated/admitted thread, and successful original manager RoleBindings insertion. Generic binding, activeAdmission, imported Values and AA-CAP status are not an issuer.
+
+The incoming original call is tied to private source/offer/receipt and exact parsed parameter identity. One call is admitted per offer. Its fixed unavailable result has success=false and says no TASK session was created. Private provenance projects named-service, not A14/person authority. No base path is resolved or accepted, no managed record is written, and no retry/delivery claim follows.
+
+Final reply eligibility uses frame_write→source gate→Inner, with no role/EXEC callback under Inner. Resolution before that cut prevents bytes; post-cut bytes cannot be unsent. Existing settling/resolution behavior is preserved. A separate same-process original-attempt cell keeps actual local IO outcome when post-cut closure prevents canonical settlement. It confers no current capability after closure, no cold hydration/durability, and disappears after its last owning reference drops. Canonical historical not-attempted is not the effective private outcome of an already completed local write.
+
+New validation uses bounded borrowed predicates for the exact closed input schema, not a new full native-schema validator under Inner. Existing full start/role schema checks still run at their original owner boundary and are outside the new core-workspace claim. Incoming calls have32768-byte serialization/16384-byte arguments, depth8/512 nodes/64 width,8192-byte strings/256-byte keys, bounded256-byte identities,4096-byte path,0–32 unique claim IDs and exact64 lowercase hex digest. byteLength is a nonnegative mathematical integer at most9007199254740991. Limits are development ceilings, not accepted C3 base policy.
+
+The fixed outgoing RPC wrapper is sender-constructed; its bounded params include the trusted fixed schema at depth8. Whole start serialization separately has65536-byte ceiling. Definition serialization≤4096. Admitted unavailable reply serialization≤2048; RPC identifiers beyond the private256-byte cap never enter the offered exception and use unchanged ordinary unsupported handling. Ordinary fallback response/Host history allocation is not bounded by private reply/core caps; no truncation/global transport policy is introduced.
+
+Tests are authored for actual CLOEXEC anonymous-pipe thread/start/call/reply transport, synthetic incoming frames and explicitly simulated write-error/partial settlement. No Host.start, child/cat/supplier/native App, process/signal/wait/reap or managed records. Code and allocation claims require the selected frozen-source review and coordinated filtered build window before reliance.
+
+Core storage accounting uses inline fixed-capacity H5/RPC identifiers, nine at-most256-byte boxed identifiers, the concrete Offer/ManagerOwner/CallFacts/Life/handle sizes and two Arc headers. RETAINED_BOUND is checked against16384; validation uses the unchanged PF1 fixed sort workspace plus4096 bounded auxiliary bytes, checked against65536 and the combined131072 ceiling. Tests report these concrete size bounds and exercise each budget refusal. These are requested core payload/workspace bounds, not allocator bookkeeping, the caller-owned parsed JSON, existing Host journals/registers, or existing full native-schema allocations. No additional argument tree is retained.
